      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Japanese Society of Hepato-Biliary-Pancreatic Surgery.",
        "AbstractText": "Highlight Kurtcehajic and colleagues present a rare case of congenital portal vein aneurysm (PVA) with biliopathy. Symptoms associated with PVA occur in less than 10% of cases. Imaging modalities showed the PVA partially compressing the common and right hepatic ducts. Conservative treatment markedly lowered bilirubin levels and relieved the abdominal pain."
      },
